penxr/scene/openxr_composition_layer.cpp","commit_id":"b389d580ac1f2212b344203fbd4898fb14f752db","original_commit_id":"d7490a6724d3c2811220ef9e3364b19eef5ed7b0","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Because this calculation includes `XRServer::get_singleton()->get_world_origin().affine_inverse()`, we need to run `update_transform()` any time the `XROrigin3D` is moved/rotated as well.\r\n\r\nI did some testing, and all was fine if I started the app with the `XROrigin3D` moved away from the origin and rotated. However, if I moved/rotated the `XROrigin3D` at runtime (like, when teleporting or snap turning), the composition layers would end up in the wrong spot (which can look really weird with hole punching, because the \"hole\" will be in the right spot, but the composition layer will be in the wrong spot).\r\n\r\nTo solve this, I think we'll need either:\r\n\r\n1. A way to get the current `XROrigin3D` and then watch for it to move/rotate, or\r\n2. A signal that's emitted every time `XRServer::get_singleton()->get_world_orgin()` has a new value","created_at":"2026-02-26T22:30:41Z","updated_